Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.

This type of work-work that changes the world-is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you're ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.

&nbsp;

THE ROLE

Join the high-growth Core Platform team as a foundational engineer&nbsp; building our next-generation. You will build, scale, and lead high-performing engineering teams dedicated to developing Everpure’s™ flagship FlashArray and FlashBlade storage products. Operating at the intersection of software engineering, product security, and technical program execution, you will establish the team's operational model and lead a risk-based roadmap to enhance how products are supported and improve the security posture for engineering and support. You will act independently to determine methods, procedures, and cross-functional alignment across EMEA, U.S. and APJ engineering hubs while safeguarding your team's focus time. I

WHAT YOU'LL DO&nbsp;

Drive End-to-End System Architecture: Lead the architectural evolution and end-to-end delivery of high performance, resilient storage systems from initial design concepts to high-quality shipped products.&nbsp;

Optimize for Modern Data Workloads: Design and implement robust algorithms and concurrent platform solutions engineered for modern data pipelines, AI infrastructure, distributed computing, and enterprise analytics.&nbsp;

Resolve Complex System Engineering Challenges: Apply deep root-cause analysis and system-level insight to solve multi-threaded, high-concurrency performance and reliability issues across Linux platform internals.&nbsp;

Cross-Functional Ownership &amp; Leadership: Collaborate across product management, validation, and support teams to align technical roadmaps, establish architectural standards, and drive enterprise product stability.&nbsp;

Elevate Engineering Standards: Mentor high-performing engineering peers, spearhead architecture forums, and foster a culture of technical excellence, continuous learning, and customer-first impact.

WHAT YOU BRING&nbsp;

Core Technical Expertise:&nbsp; Deep platform development proficiency in Linux system programming alongside strong hands-on expertise in C, C++, Python, Go, or Java.&nbsp;

Advanced Systems Fundamentals: Advanced Systems Fundamentals: Mastery of object-oriented design, data structures, multi-threading, synchronization, concurrent programming, and distributed systems architecture.&nbsp;

Domain &amp; Production Insight: Proven ability to make strategic architectural decisions, design for enterprise-grade high availability, and support complex production deployments.&nbsp;

Collaborative Leadership &amp; Communication: Exceptional communication skills with a track record of articulating complex system architectures, championing design proposals, and influencing key technical stakeholders.

Location: We are primarily an in-office environment and therefore, you will be expected to work from the Bangalore office in compliance with Pure’s policies, unless you are on PTO, or work travel, or other approved leave&nbsp;
WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM US:

• Innovation : We celebrate those who think critically, like a challenge, and aspire to be trailblazers.

• Growth : We give you the space and support to grow along with us and to contribute to something meaningful. We have been named Fortune's Best Workplaces in Technology™, Fortune's Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™, and certified as a Great Place to Work®!

• Team : We build each other up and set aside ego for the greater good.

